            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Bridget Anne Kelly v. United States concerns alleged fraud involving the reallocation of two traffic lanes on a public bridge for political reasons."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The dispute centers on whether reallocating public road lanes without disclosing the political motive constitutes property fraud under federal statutes."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner argues that the government is using broad federal fraud statutes to target state and local actions, alleging property fraud by reallocating two traffic lanes without disclosing the political motive."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Eric J. Feigin",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-d50d6981804f-0001-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Eric J. Feigin, the petitioner characterizes the conduct as \"commandeering fraud,\" where the defendants took control of bridge lanes as if they were their own property."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The respondent contends that a public official acting for political reasons, not personal gain, does not commit fraud by misrepresenting the reason for an official decision that is within his authority."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent Position",
